@startuml addressing
' accTitle: Opaque references through the public TypeScript boundary, with the agreed Machine calls
' accDescr: Configuration asks the first-party plugin for the windows of the application recorded at the leader. The first-party plugin converts the interaction context to a reference with a root query, queries the windows relation through the resident bridge, and the engine routes to the desktop provider, which resolves the relation and returns a snapshot whose items carry references and fields. Configuration derives rows; the chosen row's reference travels unchanged in its effect; the command executes focus on that reference, and the provider re-resolves the key, reporting unavailable if the window has gone.

skinparam backgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 18
skinparam defaultFontColor #25364B
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 12
skinparam BoxPadding 12
skinparam SequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #526B86
  ArrowThickness 1.2
  LifeLineBorderColor #B8C7D7
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #EEF4FA
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #E8F0F8
  ParticipantBorderColor #98ADC3
  ParticipantFontColor #25364B
  ParticipantFontSize 18
  ActorBorderColor #526B86
  ActorBackgroundColor #E8F0F8
  ActorFontColor #25364B
  MessageAlign center
  MessageFontSize 18
}
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
skinparam NoteBorderColor #B8C7D7
skinparam NoteFontColor #33475E
hide footbox

title Opaque references through the public TypeScript boundary (Machine calls AGREED)

actor User
participant "Configuration\n(window definition)" as Caller
participant "First-party plugin\nmachine facade" as API
participant "Machine engine\n(via the resident bridge)" as Machine
participant "Desktop provider\n(app module)" as Provider

Caller -> API: build(inputs, context)\nneeds the app's windows
API -> Machine: query("machine://desktop/", "application", {pid})
Machine -> Provider: query(root, "application", {pid})
Provider --> Machine: { items: [ { ref: "machine://desktop/app/4172", fields: {name, bundleId} } ] }
Machine --> API: snapshot
API -> Machine: query(app, "windows")
Machine -> Provider: route by the URI's authority;\nquery(app, "windows", {})
Provider -> Provider: re-resolve "app/4172";\nenumerate windows
Provider --> Machine: { items: [ { ref: "machine://desktop/win/4172/9031?title=Untitled", fields: {title, bounds} }, … ] }
Machine --> API: snapshot (JSON)
API --> Caller: snapshot
Caller -> Caller: derive rows; each row's effect\ncarries its window ref
Caller --> User: present (after the belay)
User -> Caller: choose a row
Caller -> API: command: execute(window, "focus")
API -> Machine: execute("machine://desktop/win/4172/9031?title=Untitled", "focus", {})
Machine -> Provider: execute(ref, "focus", {})
Provider -> Provider: re-resolve the remainder;\nfocus, or unavailable
Provider --> Machine: result, or MachineError.unavailable(ref, detail)
Machine --> API: result / rejection
API --> Caller: result / rejection

note over Caller,Provider
AGREED: a reference is a URI string, machine://<provider>/<remainder>; the engine routes by the authority and
never interprets the remainder, which the provider re-resolves on every use holding no queried state for callers;
the desktop remainder carries pid, window number and title because Modaliser's re-find needs the title as a
fallback. A root is a reference with an empty remainder. Nothing is cached by the engine, refreshed, retried or
made atomic across calls.
end note

' Agreed: references are opaque and provider-owned; configuration never bypasses the public TS API.
' AGREED (plugin-packages-k6): the URI encoding, the two calls, the error set and the desktop provider's remainder scheme.
' Open: cross-provider identity, an atomic instant across calls, command atomicity.
@enduml
